Chapter: VbeModeSetTest
  cites Kernel chapter VgaGraphics
  cites Game chapter Color
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Guards the sibling of main 14494: a VBE mode set activates the emulator's
 framebuffer at runtime, and it read the guest region back uncommitted,
 faulting the HOST rather than the guest. 1 alone means the mode set took
 the process down.

 `spin` is what makes this able to fail, and it reads the VBE registers
 rather than drawing. The faulting read runs on an exit counter, so a probe
 that sets the mode and returns crosses no boundary and passes on a broken
 emulator. The first version of this test got its exits from the bank write
 behind every pixel, which was fine until `gfx-put-pixel` stopped issuing
 one: the pixel path went linear, the exits fell from 1011 to 211, the
 output did not move a byte, and the guard was gone. Each `vbe-read` is its
 own port pair whatever the drawing code does, and every value is summed
 into the answer so nothing can elide it.

Section: Test

  paint : GfxMode, Integer -> Integer
  paint (m) (n) =
    if n <= 0 then 0
    else gfx-put-pixel m n 10 rgb-white + paint m (n - 1)

  spin : Integer -> Integer
  spin (n) =
    if n <= 0 then 0
    else vbe-read vbe-reg-xres + spin (n - 1)

  survived : GfxMode -> [Console] Nothing
  survived (m) = act
    print-line-uni "2"
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (paint m 400))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text (spin 200))
    print-line-uni (integer-to-text m.gfx-width)
  end

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "1"
    survived (gfx-set-mode 1024 768 32)
  end
